Z||000000||newfie||12-02-2001||08:32 AM||||First off I'm wondering what is the GM p/n for the fiero ECU?  I've heard alot of people talking about chip reprogramming, anyone used an EPROM emulator.  I want to make one, there are plans all over the net.  I beleive this would enable any fine engine tuning to be made on the fly.  Permantly install the emulator in the car, have a RS232 connection under the dash.  Anyone ever done this before?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-02-2001||10:33 AM||||You can buy eprom emulators that have all that built in.... <A HREF="http://www.digikey.com" TARGET=_blank>www.digikey.com</A>  is one source. The smallest one they have tho is for a 27256 EPROM. you'd have to make an adaptor for it to work with 2764 or 27128. You sould also use it with one of the "bank selector" adaptors described in a number of articles. <P>When used with a real EPROM the selector allow you to switch between 2 or more programs. That way you can run OE code on the street and something else at the track. It mainly for turbo motors.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
